# 6️⃣ Real Production Pitfalls (Common Bugs)

---

## 6.1 `@Transactional` not working

❌ Method is:

* `private`
* `final`
* Called internally
* Not in interface (JDK proxy case)

---

## 6.2 `ClassCastException`

```java
OrderServiceImpl impl = (OrderServiceImpl) orderService;
```

Fails for JDK Proxy.

✔ Always cast to interface.

---

## 6.3 `final` methods

```java
final void pay() {}
```

❌ Cannot be intercepted by either proxy.

---

# 7️⃣ JDK Proxy vs CGLIB – Comparison Table

| Feature                      | JDK Proxy | CGLIB          |
| ---------------------------- | --------- | -------------- |
| Interface required           | ✅         | ❌              |
| Proxy extends                | `Proxy`   | Target class   |
| Intercepts interface methods | ✅         | ✅              |
| Intercepts class methods     | ❌         | ✅              |
| Final class/method           | ❌         | ❌              |
| Memory footprint             | Low       | Higher         |
| Startup time                 | Fast      | Slower         |
| Recommended                  | ✅         | ⚠️ When needed |

---

# 8️⃣ Interview One-Liners 🧠

* **JDK proxy uses interfaces and InvocationHandler**
* **CGLIB creates subclass using bytecode**
* **Spring prefers JDK proxies**
* **Final methods can’t be proxied**
* **Self-invocation bypasses proxies**

---

# 9️⃣ When to Use What (Best Practice)

✔ Always define **service interfaces**
✔ Inject by interface
✔ Avoid `final` methods on beans
✔ Avoid self-invocation
✔ Use CGLIB only if required

